aims independent of synchronization remain available. Quota=max(0,floor(matureE*p/10000)-S); standard Universal Router initiator accounting, one-block buy maturity and cumulative E/S preserve prior sales: 1000 acquired, 200 sold at20%, then30% permits only100 more. Initial20%; USD FDV gates100K:25%,250K:30%,500K:35%,1M:40%,2M:45%,3.5M:50%,5M:55%,7.5M:60%,10M:65%,15M:70%,20M:75%,25M:80%,30M:85%,35M:90%,40M:95%;50M permanently bypasses quotas for ALL holders. A valid touch observed after a swap or at checkpoint opens the highest crossed gate permanently, without confirmation or relocking. Accepted risks remain disclosed/tested: mature shared-executor quota pooling and manipulation of either pool, including same-transaction/flash external reference manipulation, can open all gates permanently; these are not fixed. Stage1 alone means pool deployed/trading inactive. Before broadcast, establish the supported factory release service and executable owner-signed stage2, re-mine flags/salt against final initcode and real addresses, and rehearse the actual native round0 tree. Owner calls deployPriceSource for ImdSpotUsdSource, deployCompanions, tree certification, then configureAndActivate atomically with valid current price. Setup then seals; no upgrades, pauses, resets, exemptions or later rule changes. PrepareOwnerTransactions supplies wallet envelopes once real release identities/tree are available. Release record reports missing protected harness, pending mandatory platform panel, publication/attestation and actual release inputs; supplemental reviews and fork simulations are not deployment evidence. No new mainnet addresses, transactions, PoolId, explorer verification or sealed-setup evidence are claimed. See docs/mainnet/SPOT_PRICE.md and docs/mainnet/release/STATUS.json.",
